    "final_assistant_text": "Done. I created `src/textkit/slugify.py` with a single public `slugify(text: str) -> str` function:\n\n- Lowercases the input first (`text.lower()`).\n- Replaces every run of non-ASCII-alphanumeric characters with a single `-` via the `[^A-Za-z0-9]+` regex.\n- Strips leading/trailing `-` (`.strip(\"-\")`), which also yields `\"\"` for text with no letters or digits.\n- Returns `\"\"` immediately for empty input.\n\nVerified examples against the spec:\n- `slugify(\"Hello, World!\")` → `\"hello-world\"`\n- `slugify(\"  Multiple   Spaces  \")` → `\"multiple-spaces\"`\n\nI also re-read the written file to confirm it landed with the expected content.\n\nVerification caveat: this environment's evaluation policy rejects every `run_command` invocation (including the suggested `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -t tests`), so I could not execute the test suite myself. No existing files were modified, and `README.md`/`tests/` were left untouched.",
